Here's TUnit's lifecycle hook model across all four scopes:

## 1. Before/After Every Test (Method-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        // Runs before each [Test] in this class
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs after each [Test] in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void OrderIsCreated() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Per Class (Class-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture()
    {
        // Once before the first test in this class (must be static)
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture()
    {
        // Once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void Test1() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 3. Once Per Assembly (Assembly-level)

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock()
    {
        // Once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock()
    {
        // Once after all tests in this assembly
    }
}
```

## 4. Once Per Test Session (TestSession-level)

```csharp
public class SessionSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations()
    {
        // Very first thing — before any assembly starts
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDownDatabase()
    {
        // Very last thing — after everything finishes
    }
}
```

---

**Key rules:**
| Scope | Attribute | Method must be |
|-------|-----------|---------------|
| Test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `static` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `static` |
| TestSession | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | `static` |

The `HookType` enum values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) come from `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;` (or qualify as `HookType.Test`, etc.).
